    "text": "Structure of histamine<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/71aab0c5-605e-4bd3-a022-e98253c9f87b-image.png\" style=\"width: 267px; height: 182px;\" /><br /><br />Blood is slightly basic in nature (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>35</mn></math>) approx. At this <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>terminal <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;will get protonated due to more basic nature.<br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Predominant structure of histamine is<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4ccbad16-2a9b-43d6-9403-46b4581780c6-image.png\" style=\"width: 211px; height: 110px;\" />",
